Public prepared weights and tokenizer snapshot:
https://huggingface.co/DeepBeepMeep/Moss/tree/0a508e986e920c8051b99df98d27329742fc3d0e
WanGP integration portions retain the WanGP Community License 2.0 notices.
Maestro's model-local runtime, attention, progress and tiled-decoding adapters
allow this snapshot to run with the existing bundled shared interfaces.

Prompt guidance and draft-export semantics reviewed against OpenMOSS revision:
https://github.com/OpenMOSS/MOSS-Image/tree/95559c93ce9f85967de70435deefc1153a1a2fab/skills/moss-image-prompt-enhancer
Maestro's in-process compiler applies the documented top-left-pixel draft to
centered-pixel model-prompt conversion; existing compiled layouts retain their
original dialect.

Reference editor additions reviewed against WanGP revision:
https://github.com/deepbeepmeep/WanGP/tree/9905f0df941e5ec7b0c80e32555d3a61fe415726/models/moss_image
Maestro adapts the reference-isolated timestep-zero conditioning contract to
its existing attention API. No Chenkin-x GPL implementation is copied.
The original editor uses shared reference states; HQ uses the ai-toolkit
indexed reference positions, prompt-length text axis and independent guidance
branches, including the skipped negative layer. Cached K/V are per request.

